# FlexFat size-class table drift guard.
#
# The LLVM pass folds heap_select() at compile time from its FlexFatSizes.inc;
# the runtime allocates from lowfat_sizes[] in lowfat_config.c. If the two ever
# drift, a constant malloc(K) is folded into the WRONG region index, the runtime
# allocator places the object in a different size class, and lowfat_base/size
# decode it against the wrong class -- a silent miscompile (a false positive on a
# legal access, or a missed trap on an OOB one). Both come from one generator run
# (flexfat/config/lowfat-config.c emits the runtime array and the .inc together),
# and this test asserts the committed copies stay byte-for-byte identical.
#
# The pass's committed .inc must equal the committed golden .inc (pass copy is
# the current generated artifact; the parity test ties golden to a fresh regen):
# RUN: diff -u %S/../golden/nonpow2/flexfat_sizes.inc %S/../../../llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/FlexFatSizes.inc
#
# ...and the pass table values must equal the runtime lowfat_sizes[] values:
# RUN: grep -oE '^[0-9]+' %S/../../../llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/FlexFatSizes.inc > %t.pass
# RUN: sed -n '/lowfat_sizes\[\] =/,/^};/p' %S/../../../compiler-rt/lib/flexfat/lowfat_config.c | grep -oE '[0-9]+,' | tr -d ',' > %t.rt
# RUN: diff -u %t.pass %t.rt
